From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] iommu/arm-smmu: Add inherit mode for an SMMU left live
 across kexec

On the Oculus Quest 2 Linux is started by kexec from Android. The apps
MMU-500 is still in use: some stream map entries and context banks
belong to the secure world, and the storage streams depend on its
global configuration. The normal probe resets all of it.

Add an inherit mode, selected by "oculus,hollywood-apps-smmu-inherit".
The probe never resets the SMMU; it reads the stream map and reserves
every valid entry and every context bank they point at. A master may
attach only if its stream ID is in "oculus,inherit-attach-sids" and an
inherited entry matches exactly that ID with mask 0; it takes that
entry over and gets a free context bank, which is fully programmed
before the entry points at it. Entries are never freed, and S2CRs of
type BYPASS or FAULT are never written.

Every register access in this mode goes through
arm_smmu_inherit_access_ok(), which allows only what these paths need.
A read-only dump of the stream map is logged at probe and after each
attach.

Signed-off-by: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c |  13 +
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu.c      | 683 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu.h      |  33 +
 3 files changed, 705 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

